+### Time Format Compound
+
+Pass `compound: true` to format as several units glued together, using hours as
+the largest unit. The output has no spaces and no day unit, so it can be parsed
+by Go's `time.ParseDuration`.
+
+```ts
+ms(5400000, { compound: true })           // "1h30m"
+ms(91800000, { compound: true })          // "25h30m"
+ms(-5400000, { compound: true })          // "-1h30m"
+ms(999, { compound: true })               // "0s"
+```
+
+Leftover milliseconds are dropped, and `compound` takes precedence over `long`.
+Note that `ms()` can't parse compound strings back into a number.
+
